id: F24
target: src/sello/field.nim
desc: feSqrtRatioM1: final normalization inverted, 'feAbs(r)' -> 'feNeg(r, r)' -- instead of normalizing the result to its nonnegative representative (CT_ABS, RFC 9496 §4.2), unconditionally negates it, flipping the sign of every nonzero root the primitive returns. Replaces the retired F22 (its OLD target, field.feSqrtRatioVartime, was deleted by RFC-004 slice 1c) against the CT primitive's own defect class: the final feAbs normalization.
====OLD====
  feAbs(r)  # choose the nonnegative square root
====NEW====
  feNeg(r, r)  # choose the nonnegative square root
====END====
